A||||2||Ben84||SD Valve Cover???||||6||
Z||000000||Ben84||10-13-2001||04:55 PM||||Will the valve cover for a Pontiac 4 cylinder SD fit my 84 2m4???  My catalog at work has the SD valve covers with Pontiac engraved in the top of the die cast valve cover.||||reg||6
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||10-13-2001||06:13 PM||||Its been a long time since I have seen an SD-4 cover, but as I remember, it would fit, but the EGR valve might be in the way as well as clearance for the air filter. The PCV system would have to be altered slightly since there isn't one provided with that valve cover.<P>I might be wrong and I know that if I am that someone would correct me. I had looked into getting one for my 87 coupe way back when and I believe that is what I had found out. ||||reg||6
Z||000002||T-top Fiero||10-13-2001||08:41 PM||||I installed one on my 84 last year.<BR>Here is a list of modifications that had to be performed in order for it to fit a stock 2.5 setup:<BR>1. Cut down stock air filter housing to an open element style housing.<BR>2. Relocate temperature gauge sending unit from top of head to thermostat housing.<BR>3. Remove EGR valve.<BR>4. Remove decklid springs. A Rodney Dickman strut is used now. <BR>5. Remove engine lifting lug from front of head.<BR>6. Modify PCV valve to fit on side of new valve cover.<BR>7. Trim stud part of head bolt that holds brake booster vacuum line.<BR>Here are some pics.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SD1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SD3.jpg"> <P><BR>||||reg||1
